  <!--
    DEMO 03 V2 task objects and fixtures - Maintenance Kit Packing.

    V2 (AVP field test): the round bottle is REMOVED - three objects
    crowded the READY hand and blurred the grasp-strategy story.
    Two objects remain, staged on opposite sides of the workspace
    with clear approach corridors:

      OBJECT A  ReadytoUse_Rolled_Fondant_Pure_White_24_oz_box
        rectangular package 122 x 49 x 169 mm standing at
        (0.44, 0.34) -> multi-finger pinch / lateral grasp.
      OBJECT B  Craftsman_Grip_Screwdriver_Phillips_Cushion
        elongated tool 260 x 36 x 38 mm lying along +Y at
        (0.54, 0.13), cushion grip (29-36 mm across, 112 mm long)
        toward +Y -> tripod / elongated-object grasp, plus a
        coarse carry rotation into the slot (yaw <= 20 deg).

    READY-hand clearance (measured with mj_geomDistance): every
    retained object keeps >= 40 mm surface distance to all SG100
    fingertip and palm contact geoms in the demo_ready keyframe.

    Kit tray: TWO-zone industrial tray at (0.42, -0.19),
    440 x 330 mm outer.  Zone A rectangular (box target), zone B
    elongated slot along X (screwdriver target, coarse yaw).
    Dividers are 8 mm low strips; zone paints are visual-only -
    no closed pockets, no invisible walls.

    Both objects are Google Scanned Objects via
    kevinzakka/mujoco_scanned_objects (CC-BY 4.0, see
    ../scanned_objects/THIRD_PARTY.md).  Raw units metres, mesh
    scale 1.0.  Visual meshes only; collision from aligned
    primitive proxies.  Collision classes follow the frozen V8
    convention (see DEMO 01 objects header); all bodies are flat
    worldbody children.
  -->

